{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1563995-neomah-crafting-caregivers","id":1563995,"title":"Neomah crafting caregivers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-09-12T10:16:58-07:00","id":1563995,"title":"Neomah crafting caregivers","content":"Would it be reasonanle for a Nwomah to use its silver XP to craft not a guardian but a caregiver for the other babies it crafted","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-13T09:03:01-07:00","id":1564016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1563995-neomah-crafting-caregivers#post1563995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it be reasonanle for a Nwomah to use its silver XP to craft not a guardian but a caregiver for the other babies it crafted</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think neomah have very much fine control over the creatures they craft. If they should include tissue from parents that might be reasonably assumed to give the resulting infant a strong inclination for caregiving then sure, but I don't believe they'd be able to guarantee it. Indeed, if that offspring is a hybrid from such inclusions, the odds of reliably guessing how it will turn out go down. In any case, they're still not making anything that is not itself a baby.<br /> <br /> It would be a bit of an odd scenario, I think. Neomah will almost never be inclined to do it of their own accord, and if another entreat it of them, it raises the question of why that person can't just take responsibility for protecting further babies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-13T17:58:23-07:00","id":1564026,"title":"","content":"Most prior portrayals of neomah also have them stitching together patchwork kids and then just leaving them behind to go fulfill the neomah charter in another location, with new clients.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-19T21:38:52-07:00","id":1564853,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say it's impossible. But normally Neomah are delighted to make new creatures and completely disinterested in their well-being immediately after. One who went to the effort of making a caregiver for their creations of their own accord would likely be considered odd by their fellows, but while the demon courtesans have certain common personality traits, they are still individuals. They are artists in the medium of flesh, after all, and one might be interested in preserving their handiwork.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}